🚀 The feature
It'd be great that at::real would act as the identity function on real tensors.
An example is worth a thousand words (from #70253)
auto dS = is_complex ? at::real(dP.diagonal(0, -2, -1)).clone()
                     : dP.diagonal(0, -2, -1).clone();

if (is_complex) {
    at::real(dP.diagonal(0, -2, -1)).zero_();
} else {
    dP.diagonal(0, -2, -1).zero_();
}
could be simplified to
auto dS = at::real(dP.diagonal(0, -2, -1)).clone();
at::real(dP.diagonal(0, -2, -1)).zero_();
